{"task_id": "HumanEval/8", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef sum_product(numbers: List[int]) -> Tuple[int, int]:\n    \"\"\"Computes the sum and product of integers in a list.\n    Returns (0, 1) for an empty list as per requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    total_product = 1\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        total_sum += num\n        total_product *= num\n\n    return (total_sum, total_product)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/9", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Tuple\n\n\ndef rolling_max(numbers: List[int]) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" From a given list of integers, generate a list of rolling maximum element found until given moment\n    in the sequence.\n    >>> rolling_max([1, 2, 3, 2, 3, 4, 2])\n    [1, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    out: List[int] = []\n    current_max = None\n    for x in numbers:\n        if current_max is None or x > current_max:\n            current_max = x\n        out.append(current_max)\n    return out\n```"}
