entry point.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom .cli import CLIEntry\nimport sys\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(CLIEntry.main())\n\n```\n\npyproject.toml\n```toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"sort-third-app\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A library and service for sorting elements at indices divisible by three in a list.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nlicense = \"MIT\"\nreadme = \"README.md\"\npackages = [{include = \"sort_third_app\", from = \"src\"}]\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.8,<4.0\"\nfastapi = {version = \"^0.111.0\", optional = true}\nuvicorn = {version = \"^0.30.1\", optional = true}\npydantic = {version = \"^2.7.4\", optional = true}\npython-dotenv = \"^1.0.0\"\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.2\"\npytest-cov = \"^5.0.0\"\nflake8 = \"^7.1.0\"\nblack = \"^24.4.2\"\nisort = \"^5.13.2\"\n\n[tool.poetry.extras]\napi = [\"fastapi\", \"uvicorn\", \"pydantic\"]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nsort-third = \"sort_third_app.cli:CLIEntry.main\"\n\n[tool.pytest.ini_options]\npythonpath = [\"src\"]\naddopts = \"--cov=src/sort_third_app --cov-report=term-missing\"\n\n```\n\nREADME.md\n```markdown\n# Sort Third Application\n\nA Python library and service that transforms input lists by sorting only elements located at indices divisible by three (0, 3, 6, ...), leaving other positions unchanged.\n\nThis project provides:\n- A reusable Python library (`sort_third_app.sort_third`).\n- A command-line interface (CLI) for shell usage.\n- An HTTP API for integration with other systems.\n- Optional invocation history persistence to a local SQLite database.\n\n## Installation\n\n1. **Clone the repository:**\n   ```bash\n   git clone <repository-url>\n   cd sort-third-app\n   ```\n\n2. **Install with Poetry (recommended):**\n   ```bash\n   poetry install\n   ```\n   To enable HTTP API dependencies:\n   ```bash\n   poetry install -E api\n   ```\n\n   Alternatively, using pip:\n   ```bash\n   pip install .\n   # For HTTP API:\n   pip install .[api]\n   ```\n\n## Usage\n\n### 1. Library Mode\n\nYou can import and use the `sort_third` function directly in your Python code:\n\n```python\nfrom sort_third_app import sort_third, SortThirdService, SortThirdAlgorithm, Config\n\n# Using the convenient top-level function\nmy_list = [5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2]\ntransformed_list = sort_third(my_list)\nprint(f\"Transformed list: {transformed_list}\") # Output: [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n\n# Using the service layer directly for more control (e.g., without persistence)\nconfig = Config.from_env() # Loads config from environment variables\nalgorithm = SortThirdAlgorithm()\n# Create a service without a repository for no persistence\nservice_no_persist = SortThirdService(algorithm=algorithm, repository=None, config=config)\nresult = service_no_persist.sort([10, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7])\nprint(f\"Service-sorted list: {result}\") # Output: [3, 1, 2, 6, 4, 5, 10, 7]\n```\n\n### 2. Command-Line Interface (CLI)\n\nThe CLI tool `sort-third` can be invoked after installation:\n\n```bash\n# Using direct input\nsort-third --input '5,6,3,4,8,9,2'\n# Output:\n# {\n#   \"result\": [\n#     2,\n#     6,\n#     3,\n#     4,\n#     8,\n#     9,\n#     5\n#   ]\n# }\n\n# Using a file (e.g., `input.json` containing `[10,1,2,3,4,5,6,7]`)\necho '[10,1,2,3,4,5,6,7]' > input.json\nsort-third --file input.json\n# Output:\n# {\n#   \"result\": [\n#     3,\n#     1,\n#     2,\n#     6,\n#     4,\n#     5,\n#     10,\n#     7\n#   ]\n# }\n\n# For compact JSON output\nsort-third --input '1,5,3,2' --json-output\n# Output: {\"result\":[1,5,3,2]}\n```\n\n### 3. HTTP API\n\nEnsure you have installed with the `api` extra (`poetry install -E api`).\nRun the API server using Uvicorn:\n\n```bash\nuvicorn sort_third_app.api:create_app --factory --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThe API will be available at `http://0.0.0.0:8000`.\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST /sort`\n\n**Request Body (JSON):**\n```json\n{\n  \"list\": [5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2]\n}\n```\n\n**Response Body (JSON):**\n```json\n{\n  \"result\": [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n}\n```\n\n**Example with `curl`:**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"list\": [5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2]}' \\\n     http://localhost:8000/sort\n# Output: {\"result\":[2,6,3,4,8,9,5]}\n```\n\n### 4. Optional Persistence\n\nTo enable invocation history persistence, set the `SORT_THIRD_ENABLE_PERSISTENCE` environment variable to `true`. You can also specify the SQLite database path with `SORT_THIRD_DB_PATH`.\n\n```bash\nexport SORT_THIRD_ENABLE_PERSISTENCE=\"true\"\nexport SORT_THIRD_DB_PATH=\"/tmp/my_history.db\"\n\n# Now run CLI or API as usual. Records will be saved to /tmp/my_history.db.\nsort-third --input '1,2,3,4,5,6'\n```\n\n### 5. API Key Authentication\n\nTo secure your API, set the `SORT_THIRD_API_KEY` environment variable.\nWhen set, all `POST /sort` requests must include an `X-API-Key` header matching this value.\n\n```bash\nexport SORT_THIRD_API_KEY=\"your_secret_key\"\n\n# With API key\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -H \"X-API-Key: your_secret_key\" \\\n     -d '{\"list\": [1,2,3]}' \\\n     http://localhost:8000/sort\n\n# Without API key (will result in 401 Unauthorized)\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n     -d '{\"list\": [1,2,3]}' \\\n     http://localhost:8000/sort\n```\n\n## Development\n\n### Running Tests\n\nAfter installing dev dependencies (`poetry install --with dev`), run tests with pytest:\n\n```bash\npoetry run pytest\n```\n\n### Code Formatting and Linting\n\n```bash\npoetry run black src tests\npoetry run isort src tests\npoetry run flake8 src tests\n```\n\n---\n\n## Data Model (for persistence)\n\nThe `history` table in the SQLite database stores:\n\n| Column        | Type     | Description                           |\n|---------------|----------|---------------------------------------|\n| `id`          | INTEGER  | Primary key, auto-incrementing        |\n| `timestamp_iso`| TEXT     | ISO-formatted UTC timestamp of invocation |\n| `input_json`  | TEXT     | JSON string of the input list         |\n| `output_json` | TEXT     | JSON string of the transformed list   |\n\n```\n\ntests/test_algorithm.py\n```python\nfrom sort_third_app.algorithm import SortThirdAlgorithm\nfrom sort_third_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError, InvalidElementError\nimport pytest\n\nclass TestSortThirdAlgorithm:\n    \"\"\"Tests for the SortThirdAlgorithm class.\"\"\"\n\n    def setup_method(self):\n        \"\"\"Setup method for tests.\"\"\"\n        self.algorithm = SortThirdAlgorithm()\n\n    def test_empty_list(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with an empty list.\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([]) == []\n\n    def test_single_element_list(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with a list containing a single element.\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([1]) == [1]\n\n    def test_example_from_spec(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with the example provided in the specification.\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2]) == [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n\n    def test_another_example(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with another valid list.\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([10, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7]) == [3, 1, 2, 6, 4, 5, 10, 7]\n\n    def test_list_with_mixed_comparable_types(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with a list containing mixed, but comparable, types (int, float).\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([3.5, 2, 1, 0.5, 4, 6]) == [0.5, 2, 1, 3.5, 4, 6]\n\n    def test_list_with_no_divisible_by_3_indices(self):\n        \"\"\"Test lists where no additional indices are divisible by 3 beyond index 0.\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([1, 2]) == [1, 2]\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([1, 2, 4, 5]) == [1, 2, 4, 5]\n\n    def test_invalid_input_type(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with non-list input, expecting InvalidInputError.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"Input to sort_third must be a list.\"):\n            self.algorithm.sort(\"not a list\")\n        with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError):\n            self.algorithm.sort(None)\n\n    def test_incomparable_elements(self):\n        \"\"\"Test with elements at target indices that cannot be compared.\"\"\"\n        with pytest.raises(InvalidElementError, match=\"Elements at target indices are not mutually comparable.\"):\n            self.algorithm.sort([1, 2, 3, \"a\", 5, 6])\n        with pytest.raises(InvalidElementError):\n            self.algorithm.sort([{\"key\": 1}, 2, 3])\n\n    def test_only_first_element_sorted(self):\n        \"\"\"Test a scenario where only the first element (index 0) is sorted.\"\"\"\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([5, 2, 3]) == [5, 2, 3]\n        assert self.algorithm.sort([10, 2, 3, 1, 5, 6, 0]) == [0, 2, 3, 1, 5, 6, 10]\n\n```\n\ntests/test_service.py\n```python\nfrom sort_third_app.service import SortThirdService\nfrom sort_third_app.algorithm import SortThirdAlgorithm\nfrom sort_third_app.repository import HistoryRepository\nfrom sort_third_app.config import Config, DEFAULT_DB_PATH\nfrom sort_third_app.exceptions import InvalidInputError, InvalidElementError, PersistenceError\nfrom sort_third_app.models import HistoryRecord\nimport pytest\nfrom unittest.mock import Mock, patch\nimport datetime\nimport json\n\nclass TestSortThirdService:\n    \"\"\"Tests for the SortThirdService class.\"\"\"\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def algorithm_mock(self):\n        \"\"\"Mock for SortThirdAlgorithm.\"\"\"\n        mock = Mock(spec=SortThirdAlgorithm)\n        mock.sort.side_effect = lambda x: x # Default: return input, to be overridden for specific tests\n        return mock\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def repository_mock(self):\n        \"\"\"Mock for HistoryRepository.\"\"\"\n        mock = Mock(spec=HistoryRepository)\n        mock.save.return_value = 1\n        return mock\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def config_enabled(self):\n        \"\"\"Config with persistence enabled.\"\"\"\n        return Config(db_path=DEFAULT_DB_PATH, enable_persistence=True, api_key=None, debug=False)\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def config_disabled(self):\n        \"\"\"Config with persistence disabled.\"\"\"\n        return Config(db_path=DEFAULT_DB_PATH, enable_persistence=False, api_key=None, debug=False)\n\n    @pytest.fixture\n    def config_debug(self):\n        \"\"\"Config with debug mode enabled.\"\"\"\n        return Config(db_path=DEFAULT_DB_PATH, enable_persistence=True, api_key=None, debug=True)\n\n    def test_sort_delegates_to_algorithm(self, algorithm_mock, config_disabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify sort method delegates to the algorithm.\"\"\"\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, None, config_disabled)\n        test_list = [1, 2, 3]\n        service.sort(test_list)\n        algorithm_mock.sort.assert_called_once_with(test_list)\n\n    def test_sort_returns_algorithm_result(self, algorithm_mock, config_disabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify sort method returns the result from the algorithm.\"\"\"\n        algorithm_mock.sort.return_value = [3, 2, 1]\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, None, config_disabled)\n        result = service.sort([1, 2, 3])\n        assert result == [3, 2, 1]\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_calls_sort(self, algorithm_mock, config_disabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify sort_and_record calls the internal sort logic.\"\"\"\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, None, config_disabled)\n        test_list = [1, 2, 3]\n        service.sort_and_record(test_list)\n        algorithm_mock.sort.assert_called_once_with(test_list)\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_persists_when_enabled(self, algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_enabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify persistence is called when enabled.\"\"\"\n        algorithm_mock.sort.return_value = [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_enabled)\n        test_list = [5, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 2]\n\n        with patch('datetime.datetime') as mock_dt:\n            mock_dt.utcnow.return_value = datetime.datetime(2023, 1, 1, 12, 0, 0)\n            mock_dt.utcnow.isoformat.return_value = \"2023-01-01T12:00:00\"\n            result = service.sort_and_record(test_list)\n\n            assert result == [2, 6, 3, 4, 8, 9, 5]\n            repository_mock.save.assert_called_once()\n            args, kwargs = repository_mock.save.call_args\n            saved_record: HistoryRecord = args[0]\n            assert saved_record.timestamp_iso == \"2023-01-01T12:00:00\"\n            assert json.loads(saved_record.input_json) == test_list\n            assert json.loads(saved_record.output_json) == result\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_does_not_persist_when_disabled(self, algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_disabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify persistence is not called when disabled.\"\"\"\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_disabled)\n        service.sort_and_record([1, 2, 3])\n        repository_mock.save.assert_not_called()\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_persistence_failure_fail_open(self, algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_enabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify persistence failure is logged but doesn't raise if not in debug.\"\"\"\n        repository_mock.save.side_effect = PersistenceError(\"DB error\")\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_enabled)\n        test_list = [1, 2, 3]\n\n        with patch('sort_third_app.service.logger.error') as mock_logger_error:\n            result = service.sort_and_record(test_list)\n            assert result == test_list\n            mock_logger_error.assert_called_once()\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_persistence_failure_raises_in_debug(self, algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_debug):\n        \"\"\"Verify persistence failure raises if in debug mode.\"\"\"\n        repository_mock.save.side_effect = PersistenceError(\"DB error in debug\")\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_debug)\n        test_list = [1, 2, 3]\n\n        with pytest.raises(PersistenceError, match=\"DB error in debug\"):\n            service.sort_and_record(test_list)\n\n    def test_sort_raises_invalid_input_error(self, algorithm_mock, config_disabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify sort method raises InvalidInputError for non-list input.\"\"\"\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, None, config_disabled)\n        with pytest.raises(InvalidInputError, match=\"Input data must be a Python list.\"):\n            service.sort(\"not a list\")\n\n    def test_sort_raises_invalid_element_error(self, algorithm_mock, config_disabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify sort method raises InvalidElementError from algorithm.\"\"\"\n        algorithm_mock.sort.side_effect = InvalidElementError(\"Incomparable types\")\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, None, config_disabled)\n        with pytest.raises(InvalidElementError, match=\"Incomparable types\"):\n            service.sort([1, 2, \"a\"])\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_handles_unexpected_persistence_error(self, algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_enabled):\n        \"\"\"Verify sort_and_record logs unexpected persistence errors but doesn't raise.\"\"\"\n        repository_mock.save.side_effect = Exception(\"Unknown DB error\")\n        service = SortThirdService(algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_enabled)\n        test_list = [1, 2, 3]\n\n        with patch('sort_third_app.service.logger.error') as mock_logger_error:\n            result = service.sort_and_record(test_list)\n            assert result == test_list\n            mock_logger_error.assert_called_once()\n            assert \"Unexpected error during persistence\" in mock_logger_error.call_args[0][0]\n\n    def test_sort_and_record_unexpected_persistence_error_raises_in_debug(self, algorithm_mock, repository_mock, config_debug):\n        \"\"\"Verify