{"task_id": "HumanEval/54", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[project]\nname = \"samechars\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A library and service to check if two strings contain the same set of characters.\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.9\"\nauthors = [\n    { name = \"Your Name\", email = \"your.email@example.com\" },\n]\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=61.0\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project.entry-points.\"console_scripts\"]\nsamechars-cli = \"samechars:cli_main\"\n\n[project.optional-dependencies]\ndev = [\n    \"pytest>=7.0\",\n    \"gunicorn>=20.1\", # For easily running the WSGI app\n]\n```\n\n```markdown\n# README.md\n# SameChars Library and Service\n\nThis project provides a Python library, CLI tool, and a lightweight WSGI HTTP API to determine if two input strings contain exactly the same set of characters.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install samechars\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### Library\n\n```python\nfrom samechars import same_chars, make_default_service, StringNormalizer\n\n# Convenience function with default settings (case-sensitive, cached)\nprint(same_chars('eabcdzzzz', 'dddzzzzzzzddeddabc')) # True\nprint(same_chars('A', 'a')) # False (case-sensitive by default)\n\n# With custom service configuration\nnormalizer = StringNormalizer(case_sensitive=False)\nservice = make_default_service(normalizer=normalizer)\nprint(service.same_chars('A', 'a')) # True (case-insensitive)\n```\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\nsamechars-cli \"hello\" \"olleh\" # Prints True, exits 0\nsamechars-cli \"hello\" \"world\" # Prints False, exits 1\nsamechars-cli \"Hello\" \"hello\" # Prints False (case-sensitive by default)\n```\n\n### HTTP API\n\nThe WSGI application can be run with any WSGI server, e.g., `wsgiref` for development or `gunicorn` for production.\n\n**Development server (wsgiref):**\n\n```python\nfrom wsgiref.simple_server import make_server\nfrom samechars import wsgi_app\n\nwith make_server('', 8000, wsgi_app) as httpd:\n    print(\"Serving on port 8000...\")\n    httpd.serve_forever()\n```\n\n**Using cURL:**\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"s0\": \"eabcdzzzz\", \"s1\": \"dddzzzzzzzddeddabc\"}' http://localhost:8000/samechars\n# {\"result\": true}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"s0\": \"hello\", \"s1\": \"world\"}' http://localhost:8000/samechars\n# {\"result\": false}\n\ncurl -X POST -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"s0\": \"A\", \"s1\": \"a\"}' http://localhost:8000/samechars\n# {\"result\": false}\n```\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/models.py\nfrom typing import Iterable\n\nclass CharSetModel:\n    \"\"\"Immutable representation of a normalized set of characters.\"\"\"\n    chars: frozenset[str]\n\n    def __init__(self, chars: Iterable[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Construct frozenset from iterable of characters.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(chars, Iterable):\n            raise TypeError(\"Chars must be an iterable.\")\n        self.chars = frozenset(chars)\n\n    def to_frozenset(self) -> frozenset[str]:\n        \"\"\"Return underlying frozenset.\"\"\"\n        return self.chars\n\n    def __eq__(self, other: object) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Equality based on frozenset equality.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(other, CharSetModel):\n            return NotImplemented\n        return self.chars == other.chars\n\n    def __hash__(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Hash based on the frozenset.\"\"\"\n        return hash(self.chars)\n\n    def __repr__(self) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Debug-friendly representation.\"\"\"\n        return f\"CharSetModel(chars={self.chars!r})\"\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/normalizer.py\nfrom typing import Iterable\n\nDEFAULT_CASE_SENSITIVE: bool = True\n\nclass StringNormalizer:\n    \"\"\"Converts raw input strings to canonical characters according to policy.\"\"\"\n    case_sensitive: bool\n\n    def __init__(self, case_sensitive: bool = DEFAULT_CASE_SENSITIVE) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Create normalizer with configurable case sensitivity.\"\"\"\n        self.case_sensitive = case_sensitive\n\n    def normalize(self, s: str) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Return normalized string, applying case folding if configured.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(s, str):\n            raise TypeError(\"Input 's' must be a string.\")\n        return s if self.case_sensitive else s.lower()\n\n    def normalized_chars(self, s: str) -> Iterable[str]:\n        \"\"\"Yield normalized characters as one-character strings.\"\"\"\n        normalized_s = self.normalize(s)\n        return normalized_s\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/repositories.py\nfrom abc import ABC, abstractmethod\nfrom collections import OrderedDict\nfrom typing import Optional, frozenset\n\nDEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE: int = 1024\n\nclass CacheRepository(ABC):\n    \"\"\"Abstract cache interface for string to frozenset mapping.\"\"\"\n    @abstractmethod\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[frozenset[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieve a value by key, or None if not present.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def set(self, key: str, value: frozenset[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Store a value for a given key.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\n    @abstractmethod\n    def size(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the current number of entries in the cache.\"\"\"\n        pass\n\nclass InMemoryCacheRepository(CacheRepository):\n    \"\"\"LRU in-memory cache for mapping input string to frozenset of chars.\"\"\"\n    _max_entries: int\n    _store: OrderedDict[str, frozenset[str]]\n\n    def __init__(self, max_entries: int = DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initialize the cache with a maximum capacity.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(max_entries, int) or max_entries <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"max_entries must be a positive integer.\")\n        self._max_entries = max_entries\n        self._store = OrderedDict()\n\n    def get(self, key: str) -> Optional[frozenset[str]]:\n        \"\"\"Return value if present, moving key to end to mark as MRU.\"\"\"\n        if key in self._store:\n            value = self._store.pop(key)  # Remove and re-insert to mark as MRU\n            self._store[key] = value\n            return value\n        return None\n\n    def set(self, key: str, value: frozenset[str]) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Insert value, evict LRU if over capacity.\"\"\"\n        if key in self._store:\n            self._store.pop(key)  # Remove existing entry to update its position\n        self._store[key] = value\n\n        if len(self._store) > self._max_entries:\n            self._store.popitem(last=False)  # Evict LRU item\n\n    def size(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Return the current number of entries.\"\"\"\n        return len(self._store)\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/exceptions.py\nclass SameCharsError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base exception for the samechars library.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InvalidInputError(SameCharsError, ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Raised for invalid input specific errors.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/utils.py\nimport json\nfrom typing import Any, Tuple, Dict\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError\n\ndef ensure_str(value: Any, name: str = \"value\") -> str:\n    \"\"\"Validate value is str; else raise InvalidInputError.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(value, str):\n        raise InvalidInputError(f\"'{name}' must be a string, but received {type(value).__name__}.\")\n    return value\n\ndef json_response(status: int, payload: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[str, Dict[str, str], bytes]:\n    \"\"\"Helper to format WSGI response, returning status string, headers, and body.\"\"\"\n    status_msg = {\n        200: \"200 OK\",\n        400: \"400 Bad Request\",\n        404: \"404 Not Found\",\n        405: \"405 Method Not Allowed\",\n        413: \"413 Payload Too Large\",\n        500: \"500 Internal Server Error\",\n    }.get(status, f\"{status} Unknown Status\")\n    headers = {'Content-Type': 'application/json'}\n    body = json.dumps(payload).encode('utf-8')\n    return status_msg, headers, body\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/services.py\nfrom typing import frozenset\nfrom .normalizer import StringNormalizer\nfrom .repositories import CacheRepository\nfrom .utils import ensure_str\n\nclass SameCharsService:\n    \"\"\"Coordinates normalization, caching, and character set equality comparison.\"\"\"\n    normalizer: StringNormalizer\n    cache: CacheRepository\n\n    def __init__(self, normalizer: StringNormalizer, cache: CacheRepository) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Dependency injection to support testability.\"\"\"\n        self.normalizer = normalizer\n        self.cache = cache\n\n    def same_chars(self, s0: str, s1: str) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Public API to check if two strings have the same unique character set.\"\"\"\n        s0 = ensure_str(s0, \"s0\")\n        s1 = ensure_str(s1, \"s1\")\n        fs0 = self._chars_for(s0)\n        fs1 = self._chars_for(s1)\n        return fs0 == fs1\n\n    def _chars_for(self, s: str) -> frozenset[str]:\n        \"\"\"Internal helper: check cache, else compute normalized characters, cache, and return.\"\"\"\n        cached = self.cache.get(s)\n        if cached is not None:\n            return cached\n        chars = frozenset(self.normalizer.normalized_chars(s))\n        self.cache.set(s, chars)\n        return chars\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/controllers.py\nimport sys\nimport json\nfrom typing import Sequence, Callable, Iterable as TIterable, Tuple, Any\nfrom .services import SameCharsService\nfrom .exceptions import InvalidInputError, SameCharsError\nfrom .utils import ensure_str, json_response\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Exposes CLI for callers to compare character sets.\"\"\"\n    service: SameCharsService\n\n    def __init__(self, service: SameCharsService) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initialize with a SameCharsService instance.\"\"\"\n        self.service = service\n\n    def _print_result(self, result: bool) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Prints the boolean result to stdout.\"\"\"\n        print(\"True\" if result else \"False\")\n\n    def run(self, argv: Sequence[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Parse arguments, call service, print result, and return exit code.\"\"\"\n        if len(argv) != 2:\n            print(\"Usage: samechars-cli <s0> <s1>\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        s0, s1 = argv[0], argv[1]\n        try:\n            result = self.service.same_chars(s0, s1)\n            self._print_result(result)\n            return 0 if result else 1\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2\n        except SameCharsError as e:\n            print(f\"An application error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n        except Exception:\n            print(\"An unexpected error occurred.\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1\n\n\nclass ApiController:\n    \"\"\"Provides WSGI application for POST /samechars endpoint.\"\"\"\n    service: SameCharsService\n\n    def __init__(self, service: SameCharsService) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Initialize with a SameCharsService instance.\"\"\"\n        self.service = service\n\n    def _parse_request(self, environ: dict) -> Tuple[str, str]:\n        \"\"\"Extract s0 and s1 from the request body.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            request_body_size = int(environ.get('CONTENT_LENGTH', 0) or 0)\n            if request_body_size > 1024 * 1024:  # Limit to 1MB\n                raise InvalidInputError(\"Payload too large.\")\n\n            request_body = environ['wsgi.input'].read(request_body_size) if request_body_size else b''\n            data = json.loads(request_body.decode('utf-8') or '{}')\n\n            s0 = ensure_str(data.get('s0'), 's0')\n            s1 = ensure_str(data.get('s1'), 's1')\n            return s0, s1\n        except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Malformed JSON: {e}\")\n        except KeyError as e:\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"Missing required field: {e}\")\n        except UnicodeDecodeError:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Invalid UTF-8 in request body.\")\n\n    def wsgi_app(self, environ: dict, start_response: Callable) -> TIterable[bytes]:\n        \"\"\"WSGI callable: parses request, validates, calls service, returns JSON response.\"\"\"\n        if environ['REQUEST_METHOD'] != 'POST':\n            status, headers, body = json_response(405, {'error': 'Method Not Allowed'})\n            start_response(status, list(headers.items()))\n            return [body]\n        \n        if environ.get('PATH_INFO') != '/samechars':\n            status, headers, body = json_response(404, {'error': 'Not Found'})\n            start_response(status, list(headers.items()))\n            return [body]\n\n        try:\n            s0, s1 = self._parse_request(environ)\n            result = self.service.same_chars(s0, s1)\n            status, headers, body = json_response(200, {'result': result})\n            start_response(status, list(headers.items()))\n            return [body]\n        except InvalidInputError as e:\n            status, headers, body = json_response(400, {'error': str(e)})\n            start_response(status, list(headers.items()))\n            return [body]\n        except SameCharsError as e:\n            status, headers, body = json_response(500, {'error': f\"Application error: {e}\"})\n            start_response(status, list(headers.items()))\n            return [body]\n        except Exception as e:\n            status, headers, body = json_response(500, {'error': f\"Internal server error: {e}\"})\n            start_response(status, list(headers.items()))\n            return [body]\n\n```\n\n```python\n# src/samechars/__init__.py\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Optional, Sequence, Callable, Iterable as TIterable\n\n# Import core components to make them available for direct import from package\nfrom .models import CharSetModel\nfrom .normalizer import StringNormalizer, DEFAULT_CASE_SENSITIVE\nfrom .repositories import CacheRepository, InMemoryCacheRepository, DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE\nfrom .services import SameCharsService\nfrom .controllers import CLIController, ApiController\nfrom .exceptions import SameCharsError, InvalidInputError\nfrom .utils import ensure_str # Ensure utils are part of the available context\n\n__all__ = [\n    \"same_chars\",\n    \"make_default_service\",\n    \"cli_main\",\n    \"wsgi_app\",\n    \"CharSetModel\",\n    \"StringNormalizer\",\n    \"CacheRepository\",\n    \"InMemoryCacheRepository\",\n    \"SameCharsService\",\n    \"CLIController\",\n    \"ApiController\",\n    \"SameCharsError\",\n    \"InvalidInputError\",\n]\n\n_DEFAULT_SERVICE: Optional[SameCharsService] = None\n\ndef make_default_service(\n    case_sensitive: bool = DEFAULT_CASE_SENSITIVE,\n    cache_max_entries: int = DEFAULT_CACHE_SIZE,\n    normalizer: Optional[StringNormalizer] = None,\n    cache: Optional[CacheRepository] = None\n) -> SameCharsService:\n    \"\"\"Factory function to create a SameCharsService with default dependencies.\"\"\"\n    _normalizer = normalizer if normalizer is not None else StringNormalizer(case_sensitive=case_sensitive)\n    _cache = cache if cache is not None else InMemoryCacheRepository(max_entries=cache_max_entries)\n    return SameCharsService(normalizer=_normalizer, cache=_cache)\n\ndef get_default_service() -> SameCharsService:\n    \"\"\"Returns a singleton instance of the default SameCharsService.\"\"\"\n    global _DEFAULT_SERVICE\n    if _DEFAULT_SERVICE is None:\n        _DEFAULT_SERVICE = make_default_service()\n    return _DEFAULT_SERVICE\n\ndef same_chars(s0: str, s1: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Convenience function for checking character set equivalence using the default service.\"\"\"\n    service = get_default_service()\n    return service.same_chars(s0, s1)\n\ndef cli_main() -> int:\n    \"\"\"Entry point for the command-line interface.\"\"\"\n    controller = CLIController(service=get_default_service())\n    return controller.run(sys.argv[1:])\n\n_api_controller_instance: Optional[ApiController] = None\n\ndef wsgi_app(environ: dict, start_response: Callable) -> TIterable[bytes]:\n    \"\"\"WSGI application entry point.\"\"\"\n    global _api_controller_instance\n    if _api_controller_instance is None:\n        _api_controller_instance = ApiController(service=get_default_service())\n    return _api_controller_instance.wsgi_app(environ, start_response)\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/53", "solution": "```python\n# pyproject.toml\n[tool.poetry]\nname = \"simplecalc\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"A small, well-tested Python arithmetic library focused on addition.\"\nauthors = [\"Your Name <you@example.com>\"]\nreadme = \"README.md\"\n\n[tool.poetry.dependencies]\npython = \">=3.9,<4.0\"\nfastapi = \"^0.111.0\"\nuvicorn = {extras = [\"standard\"], version = \"^0.29.0\"}\npydantic = \"^2.7.1\"\npydantic-settings = \"^2.2.1\"\n\n\n[tool.poetry.group.dev.dependencies]\npytest = \"^8.2.1\"\nmypy = \"^1.10.0\"\nblack = \"^24.4.2\"\nisort = \"^5.13.2\"\n\n[tool.poetry.scripts]\nsimplecalc = \"simplecalc.main:cli_entrypoint\"\n\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"poetry-core\"]\nbuild-backend = \"poetry.core.masonry.api\"\n\n```\n```python\n# README.md\n# SimpleCalc\n\nA small, well-tested Python arithmetic library focused on addition. It provides a direct function call, a command-line interface (CLI), and a minimal REST API. Operation history is persisted with swappable backends (in-memory for tests, SQLite for production).\n\n## Features\n\n- **Core `add` function**: Simple, pure Python arithmetic.\n- **CLI**: `simplecalc add X Y`\n- **REST API**: `POST /calc/add`\n- **Persistence**: In-memory and SQLite history repositories.\n- **Robustness**: Type hints, comprehensive tests, and clear separation of concerns.\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install simplecalc\n```\n\n## Usage\n\n### CLI\n\n```bash\nsimplecalc add 2 3\n# Output: 5\n```\n\n### REST API\n\nRun the API:\n```bash\nuvicorn simplecalc.main:get_asgi_app --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000\n```\n\nThen, from another terminal:\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8000/calc/add -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" -d '{\"x\": 2, \"y\": 3}'\n# Output: {\"result\":5,\"entry_id\":1}\n```\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\n# Clone the repository\ngit clone <your-repo-url>\ncd simplecalc\n\n# Install dependencies\npoetry install\n\n# Run tests\npoetry run pytest\n\n# Run type checking\npoetry run mypy src\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nSet environment variables to configure persistence:\n- `SIMPLECALC_USE_SQLITE`: Set to `true` to enable SQLite persistence (default: `false`).\n- `SIMPLECALC_DB_PATH`: Path to the SQLite database file (default: `simplecalc_history.db`).\n```\n\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/__init__.py\n\"\"\"SimpleCalc package for arithmetic operations with CLI and API.\"\"\"\n\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\n# Import key modules for easier access if desired, though explicit imports are often preferred.\n# from .add import AddModule\n# from .services import CalculatorService\n# from .repositories import HistoryRepository, InMemoryHistoryRepository\n# from .sqlite_adapter import SqliteHistoryRepository\n# from .controllers import CLIController, APIController\n# from .models import HistoryEntry, OperationRequest, OperationResult\n# from .exceptions import ServiceError, RepositoryError, ValidationError\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/add.py\nclass AddModule:\n    \"\"\"Provides core arithmetic functions.\"\"\"\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def add(x: int, y: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Add two numbers x and y.\n        This function assumes validated integer inputs for direct computation.\n        >>> AddModule.add(2, 3)\n        5\n        >>> AddModule.add(5, 7)\n        12\n        \"\"\"\n        return x + y\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/models.py\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Optional\n\nTABLE_NAME = \"history\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass HistoryEntry:\n    \"\"\"Represents a persisted arithmetic operation.\"\"\"\n    id: Optional[int]\n    operation: str\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    result: int\n    timestamp: datetime = datetime.utcnow()\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> dict:\n        \"\"\"Converts the HistoryEntry to a dictionary suitable for JSON serialization.\"\"\"\n        return {\n            \"id\": self.id,\n            \"operation\": self.operation,\n            \"x\": self.x,\n            \"y\": self.y,\n            \"result\": self.result,\n            \"timestamp\": self.timestamp.isoformat(),\n        }\n\n@dataclass\nclass OperationRequest:\n    \"\"\"Input parameters for an arithmetic operation.\"\"\"\n    x: int\n    y: int\n    op: str # e.g., \"add\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass OperationResult:\n    \"\"\"Result of an arithmetic operation, including history ID.\"\"\"\n    result: int\n    entry_id: Optional[int] # ID of the persisted history entry\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/exceptions.py\nclass SimpleCalcError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Base class for custom exceptions in SimpleCalc.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass ServiceError(SimpleCalcError):\n    \"\"\"Exception for failures in the application service layer.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass RepositoryError(SimpleCalcError):\n    \"\"\"Exception for failures in the persistence layer.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass ValidationError(SimpleCalcError):\n    \"\"\"Exception for input validation failures.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/validators.py\nfrom typing import Any\nfrom simplecalc.exceptions import ValidationError\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Provides methods for validating and coercing inputs.\"\"\"\n\n    def validate_int(self, value: Any) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Validates if a value can be coerced to an integer.\"\"\"\n        if value is None:\n            raise ValidationError(\"Input cannot be None.\")\n        try:\n            return int(value)\n        except (TypeError, ValueError) as e:\n            raise ValidationError(f\"Invalid input: '{value}' cannot be converted to integer.\") from e\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/repositories.py\nimport collections\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import List, Optional, Protocol, Dict, Deque\nfrom simplecalc.models import HistoryEntry\nfrom simplecalc.exceptions import RepositoryError\n\nclass HistoryRepository(Protocol):\n    \"\"\"Defines the interface for history persistence.\"\"\"\n    def persist(self, entry: HistoryEntry) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Persists a history entry and returns its ID.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    def get_by_id(self, entry_id: int) -> Optional[HistoryEntry]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a history entry by its ID.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\n    def recent(self, limit: int) -> List[HistoryEntry]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of recent history entries.\"\"\"\n        ...\n\nclass InMemoryHistoryRepository:\n    \"\"\"An in-memory implementation of HistoryRepository for testing or ephemeral use.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self):\n        self._store: Dict[int, HistoryEntry] = {}\n        self._order: Deque[int] = collections.deque() # To maintain insertion order for 'recent'\n        self._next_id = 1\n\n    def persist(self, entry: HistoryEntry) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Stores the history entry in memory and assigns an ID.\"\"\"\n        if entry.id is not None and entry.id in self._store:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Entry with ID {entry.id} already exists.\")\n        \n        assigned_id = self._next_id\n        new_entry = HistoryEntry(\n            id=assigned_id,\n            operation=entry.operation,\n            x=entry.x,\n            y=entry.y,\n            result=entry.result,\n            timestamp=datetime.utcnow() # Ensure timestamp is current at persistence\n        )\n        self._store[assigned_id] = new_entry\n        self._order.appendleft(assigned_id) # Add to the front for recent\n        self._next_id += 1\n        return assigned_id\n\n    def get_by_id(self, entry_id: int) -> Optional[HistoryEntry]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves an entry by its ID from memory.\"\"\"\n        return self._store.get(entry_id)\n\n    def recent(self, limit: int) -> List[HistoryEntry]:\n        \"\"\"Returns the most recent entries up to the specified limit.\"\"\"\n        recent_ids = list(self._order)[:limit]\n        return [self._store[id_] for id_ in recent_ids]\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/sqlite_adapter.py\nimport sqlite3\nfrom typing import List, Optional\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom simplecalc.models import HistoryEntry, TABLE_NAME\nfrom simplecalc.exceptions import RepositoryError\nfrom simplecalc.repositories import HistoryRepository\n\nDEFAULT_DB_PATH = \"simplecalc_history.db\"\n\n# Schema SQL for initial table creation\nCREATE_TABLE_SQL = f\"\"\"\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS {TABLE_NAME} (\n    id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n    operation TEXT NOT NULL,\n    x INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    y INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    result INTEGER NOT NULL,\n    ts TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP\n);\n\"\"\"\n\nCREATE_INDEX_SQL = f\"\"\"\nCREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_{TABLE_NAME}_ts ON {TABLE_NAME}(ts DESC);\n\"\"\"\n\nclass SqliteHistoryRepository(HistoryRepository):\n    \"\"\"SQLite implementation of HistoryRepository.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, db_path: str = DEFAULT_DB_PATH):\n        self._db_path = db_path\n        self._conn: Optional[sqlite3.Connection] = None\n        self._ensure_schema()\n\n    def _get_connection(self) -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        \"\"\"Establishes and returns a database connection.\"\"\"\n        if self._conn is None:\n            try:\n                self._conn = sqlite3.connect(self._db_path)\n                self._conn.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n            except sqlite3.Error as e:\n                raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to connect to database at {self._db_path}: {e}\") from e\n        return self._conn\n\n    def _ensure_schema(self) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Ensures the history table and index exist in the database.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cur = conn.cursor()\n            cur.execute(CREATE_TABLE_SQL)\n            cur.execute(CREATE_INDEX_SQL)\n            conn.commit()\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            conn.rollback()\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to ensure schema for {self._db_path}: {e}\") from e\n\n    def persist(self, entry: HistoryEntry) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Inserts a new history entry into the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cur = conn.cursor()\n            cur.execute(\n                f\"INSERT INTO {TABLE_NAME} (operation, x, y, result) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n                (entry.operation, entry.x, entry.y, entry.result)\n            )\n            conn.commit()\n            if cur.lastrowid is None:\n                raise RepositoryError(\"Failed to retrieve last row ID after insert.\")\n            return cur.lastrowid\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            conn.rollback()\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to persist history entry: {e}\") from e\n\n    def get_by_id(self, entry_id: int) -> Optional[HistoryEntry]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a history entry by its ID from the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cur = conn.cursor()\n            cur.execute(f\"SELECT id, operation, x, y, result, ts FROM {TABLE_NAME} WHERE id = ?\", (entry_id,))\n            row = cur.fetchone()\n            if row:\n                return HistoryEntry(\n                    id=row[\"id\"],\n                    operation=row[\"operation\"],\n                    x=row[\"x\"],\n                    y=row[\"y\"],\n                    result=row[\"result\"],\n                    timestamp=datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"ts\"])\n                )\n            return None\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to retrieve history entry by ID {entry_id}: {e}\") from e\n\n    def recent(self, limit: int) -> List[HistoryEntry]:\n        \"\"\"Retrieves a list of recent history entries from the SQLite database.\"\"\"\n        conn = self._get_connection()\n        try:\n            cur = conn.cursor()\n            cur.execute(f\"SELECT id, operation, x, y, result, ts FROM {TABLE_NAME} ORDER BY ts DESC LIMIT ?\", (limit,))\n            rows = cur.fetchall()\n            return [\n                HistoryEntry(\n                    id=row[\"id\"],\n                    operation=row[\"operation\"],\n                    x=row[\"x\"],\n                    y=row[\"y\"],\n                    result=row[\"result\"],\n                    timestamp=datetime.fromisoformat(row[\"ts\"])\n                ) for row in rows\n            ]\n        except sqlite3.Error as e:\n            raise RepositoryError(f\"Failed to retrieve recent history entries: {e}\") from e\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/services.py\nfrom simplecalc.add import AddModule\nfrom simplecalc.models import HistoryEntry, OperationResult\nfrom simplecalc.repositories import HistoryRepository\nfrom simplecalc.validators import InputValidator\nfrom simplecalc.exceptions import ServiceError, RepositoryError, ValidationError\n\nclass CalculatorService:\n    \"\"\"Orchestrates arithmetic operations, input validation, and history persistence.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, repo: HistoryRepository, validator: InputValidator):\n        self._repo = repo\n        self._validator = validator\n\n    def add(self, x: int, y: int) -> OperationResult:\n        \"\"\"Performs addition, validates inputs, and records to history.\"\"\"\n        try:\n            xi = self._validator.validate_int(x)\n            yi = self._validator.validate_int(y)\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            raise e # Propagate validation errors directly\n\n        result = AddModule.add(xi, yi)\n        \n        entry = HistoryEntry(id=None, operation=\"add\", x=xi, y=yi, result=result)\n        try:\n            entry_id = self._repo.persist(entry)\n        except RepositoryError as e:\n            raise ServiceError(\"Failed to persist operation history.\") from e\n            \n        return OperationResult(result=result, entry_id=entry_id)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/config.py\nimport os\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom simplecalc.sqlite_adapter import DEFAULT_DB_PATH\n\n@dataclass\nclass AppConfig:\n    \"\"\"Application configuration values.\"\"\"\n    db_path: str\n    use_sqlite: bool\n\n    @staticmethod\n    def from_env() -> \"AppConfig\":\n        \"\"\"Loads configuration from environment variables with defaults.\"\"\"\n        db_path = os.getenv(\"SIMPLECALC_DB_PATH\", DEFAULT_DB_PATH)\n        use_sqlite_str = os.getenv(\"SIMPLECALC_USE_SQLITE\", \"false\").lower()\n        use_sqlite = use_sqlite_str in (\"true\", \"1\", \"yes\")\n        \n        return AppConfig(db_path=db_path, use_sqlite=use_sqlite)\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/controllers.py\nimport sys\nimport argparse\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\nfrom fastapi import APIRouter, HTTPException, status\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel\nfrom simplecalc.services import CalculatorService\nfrom simplecalc.exceptions import ValidationError, ServiceError\n\nclass CLIController:\n    \"\"\"Handles command-line interface interactions for arithmetic operations.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: CalculatorService):\n        self._service = service\n\n    def run_add(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Executes the 'add' command from the CLI.\"\"\"\n        parser = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=\"Perform arithmetic operations.\")\n        subparsers = parser.add_subparsers(dest=\"command\", required=True)\n\n        add_parser = subparsers.add_parser(\"add\", help=\"Add two numbers.\")\n        add_parser.add_argument(\"x\", type=str, help=\"First number\")\n        add_parser.add_argument(\"y\", type=str, help=\"Second number\")\n\n        try:\n            args = parser.parse_args(argv)\n            if args.command == \"add\":\n                result_dto = self._service.add(args.x, args.y)\n                print(result_dto.result)\n                return 0 # Success exit code\n            return 1 # Should not reach here for 'add' command\n        except ValidationError as e:\n            print(f\"Error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 2 # Validation error exit code\n        except ServiceError as e:\n            print(f\"Server error: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 3 # Service/persistence error exit code\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f\"An unexpected error occurred: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n            return 1 # General error exit code\n\nclass AddRequestPayload(BaseModel):\n    \"\"\"Pydantic model for the /calc/add request body.\"\"\"\n    x: int\n    y: int\n\nclass APIController:\n    \"\"\"Exposes arithmetic operations via a FastAPI router.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, service: CalculatorService):\n        self._service = service\n\n    def router(self) -> APIRouter:\n        \"\"\"Returns a FastAPI APIRouter with defined endpoints.\"\"\"\n        router = APIRouter(prefix=\"/calc\")\n\n        @router.post(\"/add\", response_model=Dict[str, Any], status_code=status.HTTP_200_OK)\n        async def add_endpoint(payload: AddRequestPayload) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n            \"\"\"REST endpoint to add two numbers and record history.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                res = self._service.add(payload.x, payload.y)\n                return {\"result\": res.result, \"entry_id\": res.entry_id}\n            except ValidationError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_400_BAD_REQUEST, detail=str(e))\n            except ServiceError as e:\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"Internal server error.\")\n            except Exception as e:\n                # Catch any unexpected errors\n                raise HTTPException(status_code=status.HTTP_500_INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR, detail=\"An unexpected error occurred.\")\n\n        return router\n\n```\n```python\n# src/simplecalc/actors.py\nfrom typing import List, Dict, Any\n\nclass CLIUser:\n    \"\"\"A minimal proxy for CLI usage in diagrams/tests.\"\"\"\n    def invoke(self, argv: List[str]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Simulates invoking