{"task_id": "HumanEval/67", "solution": "import re\n\ndef fruit_distribution(s,n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the number of mango fruits in a basket given a string describing\n    apples and oranges, and the total number of fruits.\n    \"\"\"\n    apples = 0\n    oranges = 0\n\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n\n    # Find the first occurrence of a number followed by 'apple' or 'apples'.\n    apple_match = re.search(r'(\\d+)\\s*apples?', s_lower)\n    if apple_match:\n        apples = int(apple_match.group(1))\n\n    # Find the first occurrence of a number followed by 'orange' or 'oranges'.\n    orange_match = re.search(r'(\\d+)\\s*oranges?', s_lower)\n    if orange_match:\n        oranges = int(orange_match.group(1))\n\n    return n - apples - oranges"}
