{"task_id": "HumanEval/96", "solution": "def count_up_to(n):\n    \"\"\"Implement a function that takes an non-negative integer and returns an array of the first n\n    integers that are prime numbers and less than n.\n    for example:\n    count_up_to(5) => [2,3]\n    count_up_to(11) => [2,3,5,7]\n    count_up_to(0) => []\n    count_up_to(20) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17,19]\n    count_up_to(1) => []\n    count_up_to(18) => [2,3,5,7,11,13,17]\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 2:\n        return []\n\n    # Use Sieve of Eratosthenes to find primes up to n.\n    sieve_size = n\n    is_prime = bytearray(b\"\\x01\") * sieve_size\n    is_prime[0:2] = b\"\\x00\\x00\"  # 0 and 1 are not prime\n\n    # Iterate up to sqrt(n)\n    for p in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if is_prime[p]:\n            # Mark multiples of p as not prime\n            for multiple in range(p * p, sieve_size, p):\n                is_prime[multiple] = b\"\\x00\"\n\n    # Collect all numbers marked as prime\n    primes = [i for i, prime_flag in enumerate(is_prime) if prime_flag]\n    return primes"}
