{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "from decimal import Decimal\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    '''\n    Converts a numeric string to the closest integer, rounding ties away from zero.\n    Assumes the input string is a valid number, not NaN or Infinity.\n    '''\n    # Convert the input string to a Decimal for precise arithmetic.\n    num_decimal = Decimal(value)\n\n    # Determine the sign for rounding away from zero.\n    sign = 1 if num_decimal >= 0 else -1\n\n    # Work with the absolute value to simplify rounding logic.\n    abs_num = abs(num_decimal)\n\n    # Get the integer part by flooring the absolute value.\n    integer_part = int(abs_num.to_integral_value(rounding='ROUND_FLOOR'))\n\n    # Calculate the fractional part.\n    fractional_part = abs_num - Decimal(integer_part)\n\n    # Apply \"round ties away from zero\" rule.\n    if fractional_part < Decimal('0.5'):\n        return sign * integer_part\n    else: # fractional_part is 0.5 or greater\n        return sign * (integer_part + 1)"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/99", "solution": "```python\nfrom decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_UP, ROUND_UP\n\ndef closest_integer(value):\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns the closest integer to a numeric string, rounding ties (.5) away from zero.\n    Uses Decimal for precision and consistent rounding behavior.\n    \"\"\"\n    dec_value = Decimal(value)\n\n    # Check if the number has a fractional part exactly equal to 0.5 in magnitude.\n    # remainder_near(1) gets the fractional part (e.g., 14.5 -> 0.5, -14.5 -> -0.5).\n    fractional_part_magnitude = abs(dec_value.remainder_near(Decimal('1')))\n\n    if fractional_part_magnitude == Decimal('0.5'):\n        # For numbers exactly halfway (X.5), round away from zero.\n        # The ROUND_UP mode achieves this: 14.5 -> 15, -14.5 -> -15.\n        return int(dec_value.to_integral_value(rounding=ROUND_UP))\n    else:\n        # For all other numbers, round to the nearest integer.\n        # ROUND_HALF_UP rounds to the nearest, with ties going towards positive infinity (up).\n        # This correctly handles non-tie cases like 15.3 -> 15 and -15.3 -> -15.\n        return int(dec_value.to_integral_value(rounding=ROUND_HALF_UP))\n```"}
